$DATUM 6-Amino-3',4',5',6'-tetrahydro-2'H-[3,4']bipyridinyl-1'-carboxylic Acid
tert-Butyl Ester (28). To a mixture of 5-bromo-2-amino-pyridine (26, 0.67
g, 3.9 mmol) and
4-(4,4,5,5-tetramethyl-[1,3,2]-dioxaborolan-2-yl)-3,6-dihydro-2H-pyridine-1-carboxylic
acid tert-butyl ester (27, 1.20 g, 3.9 mmol) were added Pd(PPh3)4 (0.45
g, 0.39 mmol) and KF/Al2O3 (3.6 g). The mixture was degassed for 0.5 h
and then heated at 100 °C for 2 h. The reaction mixture was diluted with
EtOAc (100 mL), filtered through a pad of Celite, and the filter cake was
rinsed with EtOAc (2 × 50 mL). The combined filterates were dried over
Na2SO4, filtered, and concentrated in vacuo. Purification by column
chromatography (1:2 EtOAc/petroleum ether) provided
6-nitro-3',6'-dihydro-2'-H-[3,4']bipyridinyl-1'-carboxylic acid
tert-butyl ester (0.75 g, 70%) as a brownish solid. 1H NMR (400 MHz,
DMSO-d6) δ 7.97 (d, J= 2.4 Hz, 1 H), 7.48 (dd, J= 8.7, 2.4 Hz, 1 H), 6.41
(d, J= 8.7 Hz, 1 H), 5.98 (s, 1 H), 5.93 (br s, 2 H), 3.94 (br s, 2 H),
3.51-3.48 (m, 2 H), 2.37 (br s, 2 H), 1.41 (s, 9 H). MS m/z 276.2 (M +
H)+.
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):NOTES
$DATUM solid-supported reagent, Suzuki coupling, KF supported on Al2O3 used
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):TITLE
$DATUM 4-(Pyrazol-4-yl)-pyrimidines as Selective Inhibitors of Cyclin-Dependent
Kinase 4/6
