$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM Synthesis of 3',4'-dimethyl-2,2'-bithiophene-5-carbaldehyde 14: A
degassed aqueous potassium carbonate solution (35 mL, 70 mmol) was added
to a degassed solution containing boronic ester 12 (4.91 g, 20.6 mmol),
5-bromothiophene-2-carbaldehyde 13 (3.28 g, 17.2 mmol) and
tetrakis-(triphenylphosphine)palladium(0) (992 mg, 0.86 mmol) in THF (150
mL). The reaction mixture was stirred under reflux for seven days,
whereas after two days another portion of tetrakis(triphenylphosphine)
palladium(0) (992 mg, 0.86 mmol) was added. After this, the mixture was
poured on water (200 mL), extracted with dichloromethane (3 × 100 mL),
washed with water (2 × 100 mL), dried over MgSO4, filtered and
concentrated under reduced pressure. Column chromatography (silica gel,
DCM) yielded compound 14. Yellow needles, yield (2.67 g, 12.0 mmol, 70%)
M.p. 58-59.5 oC. 1H NMR (chloroform-d1, δ ppm) 9.87 (s, 1H, CHO), 7.70
(d, 1H, J = 3.97 Hz, ThH), 7.21 (d, 1H, J = 4.00 Hz, ThH), 6.96 (s, 1H,
ThH), 2.34 (s, 3H, MeH), 2.20 (s, 3H, MeH). 13C NMR (chloroform-d1, δ
ppm) 182.58, 147.43, 142.07, 139.52, 136.72, 136.26, 130.15, 125.77,
121.54, 15.39, 14.02. EI mass 222 [M +] (calcd. for C11H10OS2 222).
Elemental analysis for C11H10OS2: calcd. C, 59.43; H, 4.53; S, 28.84%;
found: C, 59.18; H, 4.31; S, 28.82%.
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):NOTES
$DATUM incremental addition of tetrakis(triphenylphosphine)palladium, Suzuki
coupling
