$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM General/Typical Procedure: General procedure for C-3 arylation of
N-methyl-2-aryl-7-azaindole (Procedure C)
1-Methyl-3-phenyl-2-(p-tolyl)-1H-pyrrolo[2,3-b]pyridine (4a): A solution
of 3-iodo-1-methyl-2-(p-tolyl)-1H-pyrrolo[ 2,3-b]pyridine (100 mg, 0.28
mmol ), phenylboronic acid (38.5 mg, 0.36 mmol), Pd(OAc)2 (3.21 mg, 0.01
mmol), dppf (7.96 mg, 0.01 mmol) and Cs2CO3 (815 mg, 2.50 mmol) in
1,4-dioxane:water (1 mL, 3:1 mixture) was heated to 60 °C for 2 h under
N2 atmosphere. The reaction was allowed to cool to room temperature,
diluted with EtOAc (30 mL) filtered through celite and was concentrated
under vacuum. The residue product was purified by silica gel column
chromatography (hexane/EtOAc, 96:4). Compound 4a (62.6 mg, 85%) as a
white solid.
3-(Benzo[d][1,3]dioxol-5-yl)-2-(3-methoxyphenyl)-1-methyl-1H-pyrrolo[2,3-b]pyridine
(4e) Synthesized from
3-iodo-1-methyl-2-(3-methoxyphenyl)-1H-pyrrolo[2,3-b]pyridine (82 mg,
0.225 mmol), benzo[d][1,3]dioxol-5-ylboronic acid (41.1 mg, 0.247 mmol),
Pd(OAc)2 (2.5 mg, 0.011 mmol), dppf (6.2 mg, 0.011 mmol) and Cs2CO3
(146.6 mg, 0.450 mmol) by following procedure C. Purified by silica gel
column chromatography (hexane/EtOAc, 95:5). Compound 4e (56.5 mg, 70%) as
a white solid. mp 130-131 °C; 1H NMR (400 MHz, CDCl3) δ 8.39 (d, J = 4.6
Hz, 1H), 8.02 (d, J = 7.8 Hz, 1H), 7.33 (t, J = 7.9 Hz, 1H), 7.12 (dd, J
= 7.6, 4.7 Hz, 1H), 6.95 (d, J = 7.8 Hz, 2H), 6.89 (s, 1H), 6.75 (d, J =
8.0 Hz, 3H), 5.94 (s, 2H), 3.79 (s, 3H), 3.77 (s, 3H); 13C NMR (100 MHz,
CDCl3) δ 159.5, 147.5, 145.83, 143.1, 137.3, 132.5, 129.6, 128.1, 127.5,
123.3, 122.9, 119.9, 116.4, 116.2, 114.0, 112.8, 110.0, 108.4, 100.8,
55.2, 29.6; HRMS (ESI): calcd for C22H19N2O3 [M+H]+: 359.1390, found:
359.1380.
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):TITLE
$DATUM Direct C-2 Arylation of 7-Azaindoles: Chemoselective Access to
Multiarylated Derivatives
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):AUTHOR
