$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM General/Typical Procedure: Compound 3.
N-[(4,6-Dimethyl-2-oxo-1,2-dihydro-3-pyridinyl)methyl]-1-(1-methylethyl)-6-[6-(4-methyl-1-piperazinyl)-3-pyridinyl]-1H-indazole-4-carboxamide.
In a 25 mL sealable tube under nitrogen were combined
6-bromo-N-[(4,6-dimethyl-2-oxo-1,2-dihydro-3-pyridinyl)methyl]-1-(1-methylethyl)-1H-indazole-4-carboxamide
(100 mg, 0.24 mmol),
1-methyl-4-[5-(4,4,5,5-tetramethyl-1,3,2-dioxaborolan-2-yl)-2-pyridinyl]piperazine
(109 mg, 0.36 mmol) in DME/water (3 mL:1mL). PdCl2(dppf)•CH2Cl2 (9.8 mg,
0.012 mmol) was added and the resulting mixture was degassed with
nitrogen for 10 min. Sodium bicarbonate (60.4 mg, 0.72 mmol) was added,
the vessel was sealed, and the insoluble mixture was heated in a
microwave at 130 °C for 30 min. After cooling to RT, the solvent was
evaporated, DCM added, and the contents purified by SiO2 chromatography
(eluent: gradient 100% DCM to 80:20:2 DCM/MeOH/NH4OH). Further
purification by reverse-phase HPLC (eluent: 15% to 80% CH3CN in water
with 0.1% TFA, 12 minute gradient) afforded the TFA salt. The product
fractions were combined, volatiles removed in vacuo, and then diluted
with saturated sodium bicarbonate and EtOAc. The organic layer was
separated and the aqueous layer was further extracted with DCM and
DCM/isopropanol (80:20). The combined organic layers were washed with
water, dried (MgSO4), filtered, and concentrated in vacuo. The product
was further triturated from EtOAc/hexanes (with sonication) and the
solids that precipitated were filtered and dried to afford the title
compound. Compound 5.
N-[(4,6-dimethyl-2-oxo-1,2-dihydro-3-pyridinyl)methyl]-1-(1-methylethyl)-6-[2-(4-methyl-1-piperazinyl)-4-pyridinyl]-1H-indazole-4-carboxamide.
The title compound was prepared in a manner similar as described for
compound 3 from
6-bromo-N-((4,6-dimethyl-2-oxo-1,2-dihydropyridin-3-yl)methyl)-1-isopropyl-1H-indazole-4-carboxamide
(140 mg, 0.34 mmol),
1-methyl-4-[4-(4,4,5,5-tetramethyl-1,3,2-dioxaborolan-2-yl)-2-pyridinyl]piperazine
(137 mg, 0.45 mmol), PdCl2(dppf)•CH2Cl2 adduct (13.7 mg, 0.017 mmol), and
sodium bicarbonate (85 mg, 1 mmol) in dioxane/water (3 mL:1mL) wherein
the contents were irradiated (microwave) at 110 °C for 20 min. The final
product was collected as a white solid (120 mg, 70%). 1H NMR (400 MHz,
DMSO-d6) δ 11.53 (s, 1 H), 8.65 (t, J=4.80 Hz, 1 H), 8.40 (s, 1 H), 8.24
(s, 1 H), 8.21 (d, J=5.05 Hz, 1 H), 7.87 (s, 1 H), 7.21 (s, 1 H), 7.15
(d, J=5.31 Hz, 1 H), 5.89 (s, 1 H), 5.21 (quin, J=6.57 Hz, 1 H), 4.40
(br. s., 1 H), 4.39 (br. s., 1 H), 3.55 - 3.65 (m, 4 H), 2.44 (t, J=4.80
Hz, 4 H), 2.23 (d, J=6.06 Hz, 6 H), 2.12 (s, 3 H), 1.51 (d, J=6.57 Hz, 6
H); 13C NMR (100 MHz, DMSO-d6) δ 165.7, 163.1, 159.8, 149.6, 148.7,
148.1, 142.8, 139.3, 135.8, 132.8, 128.0, 121.6, 121.5, 119.2, 112.0,
110.4, 107.5, 105.9, 54.4, 49.1, 45.8, 44.7, 35.3, 31.2, 22.2, 22.1,
19.0, 18.2, 13.9; LCMS (ES) m/z: [M+H]+ calcd for C29H36N7O2 = 514.2930.
Found : 514.2930. HPLC purity/retention time = 100%/8.08 min.
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):NOTES
$DATUM microwave irradiation, sealed vial used
