$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM General/Typical Procedure: General Suzuki Coupling Method. To an
appropriately sized reaction vessel was added a halide (1 equiv), a
boronic ester or acid (1.1 equiv), potassium or sodium carbonate (2 M
aqueous solution, 3 equiv), palladium catalyst (PdCl2dppf, Pd(PPh3)4, or
FibreCat, 0.05 to 0.1 equiv) in 1,4-dioxane. The mixture was deoxygenated
by bubbling nitrogen through it for 5 min. The mixture was heated at 90
°C by conventional heating or irradiated with microwave at 100 °C, until
the starting halide was consumed. The reaction mixture was allowed to
cool to room temperature and was partitioned between water and EtOAc. The
aqueous phase was extracted with EtOAc. The combined organic phases were
washed with saturated aqueous NaCl. The organic phase was dried over
sodium sulfate, filtered, and concentrated in vacuo. If necessary, the
crude product was purified by silica gel column chromatography.
N-(2-Chloro-5-(4-morpholinoquinolin-6-yl)pyridin-3-yl)-4-fluorobenzenesulfonamide
(16d). This compound was prepared from 4b (2.01 g, 4.87 mmol) and 15d
(1.58 g, 5.38 mmol) according to the general Suzuki coupling method to
afford the title compound (1.71 g, 70%) as an off-white solid. MS (ESI
pos. ion) m/z: calc'd for C24H2OClFN4O3S: 498.1; found 499.0 (M+1). HRMS
calc'd for C24H2OClFN4O3S (M + H): 499.0998; found 499.1010. 1H NMR (400
MHz, DMSO-d6) δ 3.27-3.33 (m, 4 H), 3.87-3.93 (m, 4 H), 7.09 (d, J= 5.28
Hz, 1 H), 7.42 (t, J= 8.80 Hz, 2 H), 7.79-7.87 (m, 2 H), 7.998.04 (m, 1
H), 8.06-8.12 (m, 2 H), 8.21 (d, J= 1.76 Hz, 1 H), 8.65 (d, J= 2.15 Hz, 1
H), 8.75 (d, J= 5.28 Hz, 1 H), 10.87 (br s, 1 H).
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):NOTES
$DATUM microwave irradiation, Suzuki coupling reaction, alternative reaction
condition may also be used (conventional heating 90 degree)
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):TITLE
$DATUM Phospshoinositide 3-Kinase (PI3K)/Mammalian Target of Rapamycin (mTOR)
