$DATUM (S)-2'-(neopentyloxy)-7'-(4,4,5,5-tetramethyl-1,3,2-dioxaborolan-2-yl)-5H-spiro[oxazole-4,9'-xanthen]-2-amine
(23).
(R)-2'-bromo-7'-(neopentyloxy)-5H-spiro[oxazole-4,9'-xanthen]-2-amine
(22) (3.0 g, 7.19 mmol), bis(pinacolate)diboron (3.65 g, 14.38 mmol), and
potassium acetate (1.411 g, 14.38 mmol) were combined in a 250 mL RBF.
Anhydrous dioxane (40 mL) was added and the mixture was purged with
argon. PdCl2dppf (0.587 g, 0.719 mmol) was added and the reaction mixture
stirred under positive argon pressure at 110°C for 3 h. The reaction
mixture was allowed to cool to room temperature, then concentrated in
vacuo to a dark brown solid. The solid was partitioned between EtOAc (200
mL) and water (200 mL). Upon vigorous shaking in a separatory funnel, a
bi-phasic mixture with suspended dark solid was observed. The mixture was
filtered to remove solid and the solid was washed with EtOAc (100 mL).
The layers from the combined filtrate were separated and the organic
phase washed with saturated NaHCO3 solution (100 mL) and brine (100 mL).
The organic layer was dried over MgSO4, treated with decolorizing carbon,
filtered thorugh a pad of Celite and concentrated in vacuo. Purification
by chromatography through a Redi-Sep pre-packed silica gel column (40 g),
eluting with a gradient of 1-5% MeOH/EtOAc.
(S)-2'-(neopentyloxy)-7'-(4,4,5,5-tetramethyl-1,3,2-dioxaborolan-2-yl)-5H-spiro[oxazole-4,9'-xanthen]-2-amine
(23) (2.35 g, 70%) as an off-white solid. 1H NMR (400 MHz, DMSO-d 6) δ
ppm 7.70 (d, J=1.1 Hz, 1 H), 7.59 (d, J=8.1 Hz, 1 H), 6.94 -7.20 (m, 2
H), 6.92 (dd, J=8.9, 2.9 Hz, 1 H), 6.81 (d, J=2.8 Hz, 1 H), 6.47 (br. s.,
2 H), 4.14 (d, J=8.3 Hz, 1 H), 4.05 (d, J=8.3 Hz, 1 H), 3.54 -3.65 (m, 2
H), 1.30 (s, 9 H), 1.07 (s, 12 H).
