$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM N-(6-(6-Chloro-5-(4-fluorophenylsulfonamido)pyridin-3-yl)imidazo[1,2-a]pyridin-2-yl)acetamide
(13). To a 10 mL round-bottomed flask was added compound 7 (0.14 g, 0.35
mmol), N-(6-bromoimidazo[1,2-a]pyridin-2-yl)acetamide (0.080 g, 0.31
mmol),27-29 DMSO (3.0 mL), and aq Na2CO3 (0.94 mL, 1.9 mmol, 2 M). The
flask was carefully evacuated and backfilled with N2. To the mixture was
added PdCl2(PPh3)2 (0.022 g, 0.031 mmol). The flask was carefully
evacuated and backfilled with N2 again and then stirred at 95 °C for 1 h.
After cooling to room temperature, the mixture was poured into a solution
of pH 4.8 buffer (25 mL, 3 M sodium acetate pH adjusted to 4.8), and
water (25 mL) and filtered. The filter cake was washed with water (2x)
and DCM (2x) and then dried under vacuum to afford 13 as a tan solid
(0.102 g, 70% yield).
N-(6-(6-Chloro-5-(4-fluorophenylsulfonamido)pyridin-3-yl)imidazo[1,2-a]pyridin-2-yl)acetamide
(13), yield (0.102 g, 70%). HRMS calculated for C20H15ClFN5O3S1 (M + H)
460.0639, found 460.06445. 1H NMR (400 MHz, DMSO-d6): δ ppm 2.08 (s, 3H),
7.16-7.23 (m, 3H), 7.48 (d, J = 9.2 Hz, 1H), 7.65 (d, J = 2.3 Hz, 1H),
7.73 (d, J = 2.2 Hz, 1H), 7.78-7.82 (m, 2H), 8.14 (s, 1H), 8.72 (s, 1H),
10.69 (s, 1H), 11.95 (br s, 1H).
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):NOTES
$DATUM buffered solution used (sodium acetate) (stage 2)
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):TITLE
$DATUM Structure-Activity Relationships of Phosphoinositide 3-Kinase
